c798154749ad583fc1ca6fc132b1","quote":"The Company evaluates acquisitions to determine whether it is a business combination or an asset acquisition. Identifiable assets acquired and liabilities assumed are measured initially at their fair values at the acquisition date. The excess of the fair value of the purchase consideration transferred over the fair value of the identifiable net assets acquired is recognized as goodwill. Acquisition-related costs are charged to the consolidated statement of operations within general and administrative expenses as they are incurred.","context":"Business combinations","section":"Business combinations","block":958,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001856314-26-000006","form":"10-K","filedAt":"2026-02-25","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001856314","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1856314/000185631426000006/you-20251231.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/82c9d6817d3de094d0cd3abff454790cd34214a844af54fdc47854d5c9690e95.bin","sha256":"82c9d6817d3de094d0cd3abff454790cd34214a844af54fdc47854d5c9690e95"}},{"id":"260fef32e10ea42df773aa7f1aa3ccdc7a45831c24349aee945675259bb2638f","quote":"The Company’s intangible assets primarily consists of patents and acquired intangible assets in a business combination. Intangible assets with finite lives, including the Company’s patents and those assets acquired in a business combination are amortized on a straight-line basis over their estimated useful lives.","context":"Intangible assets, net","section":"Business combinations","block":960,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001856314-26-000006","form":"10-K","filedAt":"2026-02-25","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001856314","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1856314/000185631426000006/you-20251231.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/82c9d6817d3de094d0cd3abf