cutive Officer, evaluates financial performance and results and allocates resources based on the consolidated results of the Company as a whole. The Company's operations are primarily focused on growing and maintaining its secure identity network across multiple offerings in both aviation and non-aviation channels. See Note 1 for further information on the Company’s operations and services from which it derives its revenues.","context":"22. Segment Information","section":"Business combinations","block":1274,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001856314-26-000006","form":"10-K","filedAt":"2026-02-25","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001856314","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1856314/000185631426000006/you-20251231.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/82c9d6817d3de094d0cd3abff454790cd34214a844af54fdc47854d5c9690e95.bin","sha256":"82c9d6817d3de094d0cd3abff454790cd34214a844af54fdc47854d5c9690e95"}},{"id":"45f7f82b9e82628628947165514bb4e6cbbab16cce6a0ab09e4bbe3a6c65608d","quote":"Operating income and assets are managed at the consolidated level, and there are no separate components that are regularly reviewed for performance or allocation of resources. Consolidated operating income as reported in the financial statements is used by the CODM to monitor budget versus actual results, review performance and allocate resources. The Company’s consolidated financial statements within this Annual Report on Form 10-K reflect the Company’s operations for its single operating and reportable segment.","context":"The Company is organized and operates as a single operating and reportable segment, which aligns with the way the Chief Operating Decision Maker (“CODM”), who is the Chief Executive Officer, evaluates financial performance and results and allocates resources based on the consolidated results of the Company as a whole. The Company's operations are primarily focused on growing an